# EVERY FUSION PART WHOSE UNIT DIFFERS FROM THE LAYER IT IS COMPOSED INTO, BESIDE WHETHER IT
# FILES A CONVERSION. One row per crossing, `violates` where no factor is filed at all.
#
# ⭐⭐ THE RULE: cross a unit boundary and you must say what converts. `asrt:factor` is
#    `minOccurs="0"` and stays that way, because a part already quoted in the composed layer's
#    unit has nothing to convert and a factor of one there would be boilerplate with no author.
#    The moment the units DIFFER that stops being true: somebody is asserting the two are
#    interchangeable, and an assertion needs a filer.
#
# ⛔⛔⛔ AND WITHOUT THIS RULE THE ASSERTION WAS MADE BY THE QUERY. `composition/converted.sqlc`
#    reads a missing factor as one. Two parts crossed a unit boundary with no factor at all --
#    `pessoas` to `people`, and `turnos por semana` to `shifts per week` -- so the SQL asserted
#    that a Portuguese person and an English person are one unit, on nobody's authority. That
#    is a judgement this repository has twice refused to make in a query, arriving through the
#    back door as a `coalesce`.
#
# ⚠️ AND IT IS NOT AN IDLE JUDGEMENT. If one member counts heads and the other counts full-time
#    equivalents, the factor is not one and every composed figure above it is wrong by the
#    difference. Filing [1, 1, 1] with a `boundOrigin` and a provenance says a person checked.
#
# ⭐ A TYPED-ABSENT FACTOR SATISFIES THIS RULE and suspends the sum instead, via
#   `composition/unsized_conversions.sqlc`. "Somebody looked at the crossing and cannot size it"
#   is an answer; saying nothing is not.
-- asrt:Part against its composed pm:Layer's unit, per quantity they both file.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT DISTINCT x.filing, x.layer, x.violates, x.detail
    FROM (
        SELECT p.composition AS filing, p.composed_layer AS layer,
               (p.factor_low IS NULL AND p.factor_absent IS NULL) AS violates,
               format('the part %s/%s is quoted in %s and this layer in %s, and the conversion '
                      'is %s', p.part_filing, p.part_layer, part.unit, comp.unit,
                      CASE WHEN p.factor_low IS NOT NULL THEN 'filed'
                           WHEN p.factor_absent IS NOT NULL
                           THEN format('filed as `%s`', p.factor_absent)
                           ELSE 'NOT FILED, so a reader supplies one' END) AS detail
        FROM      (
            :compose(composition/parts.sqlc)
        ) p
        JOIN      (
            :compose(layers/quantities.sqlc)
        ) part ON part.filing = p.part_filing AND part.layer = p.part_layer
        JOIN      (
            :compose(layers/quantities.sqlc)
        ) comp ON comp.filing = p.composition AND comp.layer = p.composed_layer
              AND comp.quantity = part.quantity
        WHERE part.unit IS DISTINCT FROM comp.unit
    ) x
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'unit_crossing_without_a_factor'
